  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "A point is chosen uniformly at random from the interval $[0,1].$ Let the continuous random variable $X$ be the distance from the origin to the chosen point. Consider the triangle with vertices at $(0,0),(2,0),$ and $(2,X).$ Let $A=A(X)$ denote the area of this triangle.\n\nExpressing the integrand in the following equation as a polynomial, we have \n\n$E[A]={\\int }_{0}^{1}$\n{{field-1}} $dx$\n\nTherefore, the expected area of the triangle is \n{{field-2}}.",
